From 9d0a158af221b088e38708625c0aa38b9416e264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo R-S <rodriguez@schrodinger.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 16:36:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Prune exact-symmetry CIP auxiliary work

Large symmetric polycycles can spend most of CIP assignment enumerating auxiliary occurrences when an exact constitutional witness composes the required local ligand swap with an unrelated symmetry.

Retry those proofs with unrelated stereo neighborhoods fixed, record primary ties that auxiliary descriptors cannot break, extend path-fixed exact equality below the digraph root, and reuse a guarded target-path forest before residual BFS. Failed or ambiguous proofs retain the conservative traversal.

Add focused coverage for below-root ring equality and configuration-preserving root ties.
